\subsection{Register: Judge-Dependent Confound Structure}
\label{sec:negative_control}

Register shows a judge-dependent pattern: Llama-70B exhibits the strongest effect (BT 63.5\%, $p = 0.0014$; Likert n.s.), GPT-4o shows a weaker signal (BT 57.0\%, $p = 0.04$), and Qwen3-32B is non-significant (BT 55.3\%, $p = 0.076$).
GEE decomposition reveals that the register confound structure varies across judges: Qwen3-32B is originality-dominated (Orig OR $= 5.72$, $p < 0.0001$; Style OR $= 1.91$, $p = 0.046$), while GPT-4o and Llama-70B show mixed regimes with comparable style and originality effects (Llama-70B: Style OR $= 3.33$, $p = 0.0003$; Orig OR $= 3.07$, $p = 0.0008$; Table~\ref{tab:gee}).
These exploratory findings do not enter the primary Holm-Bonferroni family.

